1
00:00:01,360 --> 00:00:04,680
Hello everyone, I'm Lao Pa.
大家好，我是老帕。

2
00:00:04,680 --> 00:00:14,650
Today I deliberately found a place with a whiteboard behind me, because I want to walk you through a number with you today, step by step.
今天特意找了一个后面有白板的地方，和大家聊聊一个数字。

3
00:00:14,650 --> 00:00:36,430
What number is it? It is about a family of four in New Zealand, a family where both parents are unemployed, with two underage children. How much money can such a family receive every week?
什么数字呢？就是在新西兰，一个双失业家庭，一家四口人，父母都失业，带着两个未成年的孩子，这样一个家庭每周能够拿多少钱。

4
00:00:36,430 --> 00:00:43,820
Today, let's talk about this topic, and take a look at just how tough the situation actually is.
我们今天聊聊这个话题，看看实际上有多惨。

5
00:00:43,820 --> 00:00:52,310
First of all, to qualify as a dual-unemployed family, both people must have no savings at all.
首先，你要成为双失业家庭，两个人都要没有存款。

6
00:00:52,310 --> 00:01:01,910
Your net assets, the money in your New Zealand bank accounts, the closer they are to zero, the better it is for you.
你的净资产，在新西兰的账户里面的钱，越接近于零越好。

7
00:01:01,910 --> 00:01:19,630
But money in overseas accounts may not be traceable in New Zealand. For example, money in WeChat Pay or Alipay may not be found by the authorities here.
但是你在国外的账户里面的钱，新西兰可能是查不到的，比如微信支付、支付宝里面的钱，可能是查不到的。

8
00:01:19,630 --> 00:01:35,870
So, the money in your New Zealand bank accounts, the closer to zero the better. That means you have no house, no assets of any kind, and no savings.
所以你在新西兰的银行账户里面的钱越趋于零越好，也就是你没有房子，没有任何资产，没有存款。

9
00:01:35,870 --> 00:01:43,990
And if you have two children, then you meet the conditions for such a family, and you can receive government benefits.
有两个孩子，你就符合这种家庭，可以领取福利。

10
00:01:43,990 --> 00:01:52,490
First, once you meet all the conditions, let's work out exactly how much benefit you can get.
首先，你都满足条件了，我们来计算一下这个福利。

11
00:01:52,490 --> 00:02:05,780
For parents who are both unemployed, each person can receive about three hundred and thirty-five dollars a week. I already talked about this in the last episode.
父母双失业，每个人每周能拿到大概三百三十五左右，上一期节目我已经说过了。

12
00:02:05,780 --> 00:02:15,740
So the two of them together receive about six hundred and seventy dollars a week. That is the unemployment benefit paid to the parents.
两个人就相当于六百七十，一周，就是给父母的失业补助金。

13
00:02:15,740 --> 00:02:24,240
And what about the two children? The child benefit is about two hundred and seventy-five dollars a week.
还有两个孩子，孩子补助金大概是两百七十五左右。

14
00:02:24,240 --> 00:02:39,740
Then there is the question of housing. Since you do not own a house, you either rent a place privately by yourself, or you apply for a New Zealand government public rental home.
另外还有房子的问题，因为你没有房子，你要么自己去租房子，要么申请新西兰政府的公租屋。

15
00:02:39,740 --> 00:02:46,020
Public housing is handled by New Zealand's Ministry of Social Development, which is responsible for this programme.
公租屋应该是新西兰社会发展部负责。

16
00:02:46,020 --> 00:03:01,160
The government negotiates with landlords, the people who rent out houses, rents the house from them on a long-term basis, and then sublets it again to families who need it. That is what government public housing is.
政府和出租方、房东去谈判，把房子长期租下来，然后再转租给需要的家庭，就是政府公租。

17
00:03:01,160 --> 00:03:11,490
So there are two different situations. If you rent privately, the government will also give you an extra weekly rent subsidy on top of the other benefits.
这两种情况，如果你私人租房，政府还有额外的每周租房补贴。

18
00:03:11,490 --> 00:03:27,740
Taking Auckland as an example, that rent subsidy is about three hundred and five dollars a week for a family that rents privately.
我们以奥克兰为例，大概每周你的租房补贴，因为你是自己租房，一个家庭大概是三百零五，一周。

19
00:03:27,740 --> 00:03:37,700
If you live in government public housing, on the other hand, your rent is about two hundred and five dollars a week.
如果你住政府的公租屋，你每周的房租大概是两百零五左右。

20
00:03:37,700 --> 00:03:50,630
Public housing works on a formula. It charges you roughly two hundred and five dollars. That is the rent you pay.
因为政府公租有一个系数，大概是两百零五左右，就收你的钱，就是你的租金。

21
00:03:50,630 --> 00:04:00,230
Let's take an average rent of eight hundred dollars a week for an ordinary house as our example for the calculation.
我们就以平均八百刀每周，一般的房子每周的租金来计算。

22
00:04:00,230 --> 00:04:20,900
If you rent privately, your benefits, the unemployment benefit, plus the child benefit, plus the housing subsidy, add up to about one thousand two hundred and fifty dollars a week in total.
这样算下来，如果你自己租房，你的补贴，失业补助，加上孩子补贴，再加上住房补贴，大概是一千两百五，每周你拿到的钱。

23
00:04:20,900 --> 00:04:32,340
But you have to pay eight hundred dollars in rent, so after you deduct the rent, your family is left with only four hundred and fifty dollars a week.
但是你要付租金八百，扣除租金之后，你家庭里面只剩四百五，一周。

24
00:04:32,340 --> 00:04:46,370
If you live in government public housing, the parents' benefit plus the child benefit come to nine hundred and forty-five dollars a week in total.
如果你住政府的公租屋，父母的工作补助再加上孩子补贴，一共是九百四十五，一周。

25
00:04:46,370 --> 00:04:59,300
Your public housing rent is much cheaper, about two hundred and five dollars a week deducted, so in the end you are left with seven hundred and forty dollars a week.
你的公租屋便宜，租金大概每周扣两百零五，最后剩余的钱是每周七百四十刀。

26
00:04:59,300 --> 00:05:09,260
That is two hundred and ninety dollars more than renting privately, which shows that living in government public housing is the better deal.
要比私人租房多两百九十刀，说明还是住政府的公租屋划算。

27
00:05:09,260 --> 00:05:25,140
And for a family with children, applying for public housing should be very fast. In New Zealand, children come first, so any application that involves children is usually processed very quickly.
而且带孩子的家庭申请公租屋应该是非常快的，因为在新西兰孩子优先，有孩子申请什么都很快。

28
00:05:25,140 --> 00:05:32,890
Generally, within about two months, the government will arrange a house for you to live in.
一般两个月左右，政府会安排一个房子给你住。

29
00:05:32,890 --> 00:05:55,040
Now, let's compare that with a family where both parents work, but on ordinary incomes. If you compare them, the unemployed family actually ends up with more money left every week.
你就是没有工作的一个家庭，你要是和同样的家庭，有工作的，父母都去工作，但是普通的收入者去比较的话，你肯定是失业的拿得多。

30
00:05:55,040 --> 00:06:07,960
Because if both parents in an ordinary working family go to work, they still have to pay a mortgage. They must have bought a house, and after that, they do not have much money left.
因为普通的家庭都工作的话，你还要交房贷，你肯定买房子，你也没有多少钱。

31
00:06:07,960 --> 00:06:24,580
You have to pay the mortgage, and you also have to pay for food, plus the property tax on the house, house insurance, and a lot of house maintenance costs, all of which come out of your own pocket.
你要交房贷，还要交房子的地税，还有房子的保险，房屋的保险，还有房屋的维护费用，都是自己出。

32
00:06:24,580 --> 00:06:38,240
So, after you deduct all of those costs, an ordinary working family ends up with much less money left every week than a family that receives benefits.
所以扣除之后，你上班的，普通的家庭，比拿福利的家庭每周省下来的钱要少得多。

33
00:06:38,240 --> 00:06:45,250
In other words, working is worse than not working. That is basically what it comes down to.
也就是说你上班不如不上班，就这个意思。

34
00:06:45,250 --> 00:06:51,160
Of course, receiving these benefits also takes a certain amount of courage.
当然，拿这个福利也是需要勇气的。

35
00:06:51,160 --> 00:07:04,450
Take me, for example. I do not have that courage, to make myself completely penniless and then go and apply for government relief.
像我的话，我是没有这个勇气的，把自己弄得身无分文，然后去申请政府的救济。

36
00:07:04,450 --> 00:07:17,370
Some people say the government will not just leave you alone. It encourages you, and it arranges for you to keep working, and it gives you job training. That is indeed true.
有人说，政府是要鼓励你，安排你去不停地工作，给你职业培训，确实是这样。

37
00:07:17,370 --> 00:07:29,920
But for families who receive benefits, finding work is generally very, very hard. It is really very difficult to find a job. Why is that?
但是拿到救济金的这种家庭，找工作一般是很难，非常难找工作，为什么呢？

38
00:07:29,920 --> 00:07:37,680
Because New Zealand is a society that places a great deal of importance on credit and honesty.
因为新西兰是一个非常讲信用、讲诚信的国家。

39
00:07:37,680 --> 00:07:51,340
When you go and apply for jobs, and when you go to interviews, you definitely have to tell the employer your actual situation, honestly.
那你去投简历，面试的时候，投简历的时候，你肯定要把你的实际情况告诉企业方。

40
00:07:51,340 --> 00:07:59,460
You have to tell them that you are a family receiving government relief, an unemployed family.
你要告诉他，你是拿政府救济金的，失业的家庭。

41
00:07:59,460 --> 00:08:16,440
If you say that so bluntly, or if you write it that plainly on your CV, many employers will privately wonder whether they dare to hire you at all.
你这么说出来以后，或者你的简历上这么直白地写的话，很多用人单位会私下里考虑，到底敢不敢要你。

42
00:08:16,440 --> 00:08:37,860
For example, suppose I run a small company and I am hiring, and I find that there are many applicants, and one of them is you, a family receiving benefits. Do you think I would dare to hire you?
比如说我是一个小公司，我去招聘的时候，发现投简历的人很多，其中有一个就是你，你是拿福利金的家庭，你觉得我敢雇佣你吗？

43
00:08:37,860 --> 00:08:59,640
Subconsciously, and I am not saying this is discrimination, people may think to themselves: why are you receiving government relief? Is it because you are lazy? They may well think that way.
因为我在潜意识里面，并不是说真的所有人，也不是什么歧视，可能会这么想：你为什么要拿政府的救济金呢，你是不是因为懒惰呢？

44
00:08:59,640 --> 00:09:16,620
People may think that way, even though there is no intention to discriminate, so is finding a job not going to be very hard? The government may encourage you to find work, but is it actually easy to find work?
可能会这么想的，那你找工作是不是会很难呢？政府虽然说鼓励你去找工作，但是你找工作是不是很难？

45
00:09:16,620 --> 00:09:24,000
In the end, the government may arrange for you to work, or even force you to work.
最后，政府可能会安排你去，强迫你去工作。

46
00:09:24,000 --> 00:09:54,650
The workplaces the government forces you into are generally large companies that have some connection with the government. For example, in Auckland, there are many large companies, like the SkyCity casino, or large restaurant chains, which are very large and very formal operations, and which may have a cooperative relationship with the government.
政府强制你去工作的单位，一般都是与政府有一些关联的大公司，比如说在奥克兰，有很多大公司，像 SkyCity 赌场，餐饮店，非常大，很正规，可能政府跟它是有合作关系的。

47
00:09:54,650 --> 00:10:13,110
The government may place you in one of these large companies to work, but after you go there, if the work is hard, the company may let you go after just one or two months.
政府可能会安排你进这种大公司里面上班，你去了之后，假如辛苦的话，人家可能干个一两个月，也就不要你了。

48
00:10:13,110 --> 00:10:35,260
A company has the right to dismiss you. Even if you were placed there by the government, if the company sees that your performance is not good, it will dismiss you just the same, and after you are dismissed, you can receive benefits again.
企业是有权解雇你的，你虽然是政府安排过去上班的，但是企业看着你表现不好，照样把你解雇，解雇之后你又可以拿福利金，对不对？

49
00:10:35,260 --> 00:10:56,670
So it can easily turn into a vicious cycle. Once a person has reached that point, and has become that idle, it is very hard for them to adapt to working again. It is really, really very hard to adapt.
这就有可能陷入一种恶性循环，一旦人到了这个地步，已经懒到这个程度了，你让他再去工作，我觉得很难适应，真的非常难适应。

50
00:10:56,670 --> 00:11:18,080
In my time in New Zealand, I have met people who receive benefits. Among Chinese people, I have met several single-parent families, for example, a single mother raising three children on her own.
我在新西兰这么久，也遇到过拿福利的人，华人里面有像那种单亲家庭，比如一个单亲妈妈带了三个孩子，这种华人遇到过好几个。

51
00:11:18,080 --> 00:11:36,170
I think there is nothing wrong with them receiving benefits. One person raising three children alone is very hard work. She cannot be expected to go to work, and if she did go to work, what would happen to the children?
他们拿福利，我觉得是没有毛病的，因为他一个人带三个孩子很辛苦，他不可能去上班，让他上班孩子怎么办？

52
00:11:36,170 --> 00:11:55,000
So I think receiving benefits in that situation is completely normal. Another Chinese person I met was a woman in her fifties, around fifty years old.
所以我觉得这个拿福利是正常的。然后还有一个我遇到的华人，他应该是中年，大概在五十岁左右了，是一个女性。

53
00:11:55,000 --> 00:12:17,150
She lived in a government public rental home in central Auckland, a newly built terraced villa. I visited the place once, and it was new, a newly built terraced villa.
他是住在一个政府的公租屋里面，他的公租屋是在奥克兰的中区，是那种联排的别墅，是新的，新盖的，我去了一趟，是新的联排别墅。

54
00:12:17,150 --> 00:12:41,150
The government had taken that house from a landlord on a long-term lease, and then sublet it to someone in need, someone who was unemployed and needed relief, turning it into government public housing.
政府就给了他其中一套，那个房子应该是房东出租的时候，政府把它长期租下来，然后再转租给拿福利的、需要救济的人，把它变成了政府的公租。

55
00:12:41,150 --> 00:12:47,430
Most of the people I have met in this situation were women. Women were in the majority.
我都遇到过，都是女的，女的比较多。

56
00:12:47,430 --> 00:13:06,990
Australia is much the same as New Zealand. The only difference is the currency unit at the end, New Zealand dollars on one side and Australian dollars on the other. The amounts are similar, only the unit is different.
在澳洲跟新西兰都差不多，只是区别就是后面的货币单位，一个是纽币，一个是澳币，金额都差不多，只是单位不一样。

57
00:13:06,990 --> 00:13:16,960
So, do you think it is worse to work, or worse not to work? Let me know what you think in the comments.
所以大家觉得是上班惨呢，还是不上班惨呢？大家评论评论。

58
00:13:16,960 --> 00:13:37,270
Personally, I still rather admire the courage of people who make themselves penniless in order to claim benefits. I admire their courage, and I do not yet have that courage myself.
我反正心里面还是比较羡慕这些有勇气的人，把自己弄得身无分文去拿福利，我还比较佩服他们的勇气，我还没有这个勇气。

59
00:13:37,270 --> 00:13:43,400
Well, that is all for today. Let's leave it here for today.
好，今天就聊到这儿。

